Room: certificate errors of Room pages go to the host's interstitial.

Chrome answers a main-frame certificate error with its own interstitial
(SSLErrorNavigationThrottle defers the navigation, SSLErrorHandler builds an
SSLBlockingPage and the throttle commits its HTML as the error page). Room
shows its own interstitial (the Engine protocol's didFailCertificateCheck,
Phase 2.6a) and needs Chrome's verdict on whether the error may be bypassed:
SSLInfo::is_fatal_cert_error carries the host's HSTS and pinning state
(strict enforcement), which CEF never passed (backlog B-24).

No existing hook: the throttle and its error callback are created inside
CreateAndAddChromeThrottlesForNavigation (patch 0016's file) with this
wrapper bound in; ContentBrowserClient::AllowCertificateError only denies
the main frame in M154 and is ChromeContentBrowserClient's. //room takes the
error only for pages it wraps whose delegate answers certificate errors:
"Visit anyway" stores Chrome's decision (SSLHostStateDelegate::AllowCert)
and loads the URL again, "Go back" stops the deferred navigation; every
other page keeps Chrome's interstitial.

Phase 3.4a, 2026-10-05. //room: room/core/room_page_prompts.mm.
